workedExamples.solution_text:
For the median, set $F(m)=\frac12$.
$\begin{aligned}\frac{m^{3}-8}{208}&=\frac12\\m^{3}-8&=104\\m^{3}&=112\\m&=\sqrt[3]{112}\approx4.82\end{aligned}$
For the first quartile, set $F(Q_1)=\frac14$.
$\begin{aligned}\frac{Q_1^{3}-8}{208}&=\frac14\\Q_1^{3}&=60\\Q_1&=\sqrt[3]{60}\approx3.91\end{aligned}$
For the third quartile, set $F(Q_3)=\frac34$.
$\begin{aligned}\frac{Q_3^{3}-8}{208}&=\frac34\\Q_3^{3}&=164\\Q_3&=\sqrt[3]{164}\approx5.47\end{aligned}$
The 40th percentile $c$ has cumulative probability $0.40$.
$\begin{aligned}\frac{c^{3}-8}{208}&=0.40\\c^{3}&=91.2\\c&=\sqrt[3]{91.2}\approx4.50\end{aligned}$
All four values lie in $[2,6]$.
